INT. CHURCH-TURNED-SALOON, DRY CREEK - NIGHT

A former chapel with its pews dragged into a poker circle. A cracked stained-glass saint looks down on the cards with a beatific squint. Lantern light. Cigar haze. Wind scouring the shutters.

At the long communion table, five players sit hunched over a pot of coins, watches, and one wedding band.

A STRANGER in a gray duster slouches in the darkest corner, hat low, a glass of milk untouched in front of him. Nobody has looked directly at him in an hour.

At the table: SHERIFF DELPHINE ACHEBE-MARSH (40s, weary, star pinned crooked), BIG JASPER TUCKERMAN (50s, a belly like a barrel, a laugh like a rockslide), DOC PRUDENCE OYELARAN (60s, spectacles, neat fingers), and the barkeep OSWALDO "OZZIE" BRIGHT-RAMIREZ (30s, apron, a shotgun under the bar), who deals. Last, young TOMASZ KOWALCZYK-LEE (19, new boots, trembling hat), sweating over his hand.

JASPER
Call.

DELPHINE
Raise.

DOC
Fold.

OZZIE
Fold.

TOMASZ
(whisper)
All in.

The room goes quiet. Jasper looks at the boy. Delphine looks at the boy. Doc, with great delicacy, lifts her spectacles.

The Stranger stirs in his corner. Rises. Crosses the room. The planks complain under his boots.

STRANGER
Might I see his cards?

DELPHINE
It's not a game for spectators.

STRANGER
It isn't a game at all.

He stops beside Tomasz. Lays a gloved hand on the boy's shoulder. The boy flinches. The Stranger tilts his head and studies the saint in the window.

STRANGER (CONT'D)
Son, what's your name?

TOMASZ
Tomasz.

STRANGER
Not Tom.

TOMASZ
Not Tom.

STRANGER
Then Tomasz, I'll tell you mine. They call me Reverend Silas Orcutt.

A slow ripple passes over the table. Jasper's laugh dies. Doc's hand finds the edge of her bag. Ozzie reaches under the bar. Delphine, without lifting her eyes, thumbs the hammer of her pistol.

ORCUTT
(smiling)
This was my church.

DELPHINE
It was a ruin.

ORCUTT
It was a ruin because of men at this table.

Tomasz slides his chair back. Orcutt's grip tightens.

ORCUTT (CONT'D)
Stay seated, son. I'm only here for the ones who burned it.

JASPER
Now, Reverend...

ORCUTT
Jasper Tuckerman. You carried the lamp oil.

Jasper surges from his chair. Delphine fires. Ozzie brings the shotgun up. Doc dives behind a pew. Tomasz, white as chalk, flattens himself under the table, the cards scattering around him like snow.

The saint in the window, struck by a bullet, loses its head in a shower of colored glass.
